{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr3UuYsqpEK35wx5Y4a1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't see `auth.service.ts` in the retrieved snippets, so this diagnosis comes from the error message and how this boilerplate is usually built. I haven't confirmed it against the code, and the line numbers are estimates.\n\nThe error `needLoginViaProvider:google` is thrown at login when the stored user's `provider` isn't `email`. The provider name in the message is the stored value. A user who registered by email therefore had `google` saved as their provider. The most likely place is the register path, which creates the user in `AuthService.register`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4810c6b6-d508-4f3f-9686-e09c1820f97e","uuid":"2cdfa157-9afd-4216-a4a2-149c98996d9c","timestamp":"2026-11-08T19:51:37.380Z","request_id":"req_011Cgr3UuLxwqmg3zg8Z1cSR"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr3UuYsqpEK35wx5Y4a1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015AqL3eb6F6XjvwzVRd2UUm","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"candidates":[{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.register","start_line":150,"end_line":180,"explanation":"Email registration creates the user through usersService.create. The stored provider must be AuthProvidersEnum.email. If it is set to google (or taken from the wrong enum value), validateLogin throws 422 'needLoginViaProvider:google' for a user who never used Google. I could not see this code, so this is an inference from the error message."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.confirmEmail","start_line":185,"end_line":225,"explanation":"The report says the failure appears right after email confirmation. If confirmEmail also writes the provider or other fields, it could overwrite the provider with the wrong value. This is a secondary suspect."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.validateLogin","start_line":60,"end_line":110,"explanation":"Login rejects any user whose provider is not AuthProvidersEnum.email and reports the stored provider in the message. This is where the 422 is raised, but it is probably only the symptom of a wrongly stored provider."}],"fix":{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","description":"In AuthService.register, create the user with provider: AuthProvidersEnum.email (not google). Also check that confirmEmail does not change the provider. Then check that the user mapper or schema persists the provider value unchanged."}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":